  "estimatedMinutes": null,
  "statement": "Let \\(f(x)=x^{3}+a x+b\\), with \\(a \\neq b\\), and suppose the tangent lines to the graph of \\(f\\) at \\(x=a\\) and \\(x=b\\) are parallel. Find \\(f(1)\\).",
  "answerChoices": [],
  "answer": {
    "letter": null,
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-calculus-2005-p1.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "1\n\nSince \\(f^{\\prime}(x)=3 x^{2}+a\\), we must have \\(3 a^{2}+a=3 b^{2}+a\\). Then \\(a^{2}=b^{2}\\), and since \\(a \\neq b\\), \\(a=-b\\). Thus \\(f(1)=1+a+b=1\\).",
